General result

Your equation becomes

Peffective=ϕ(CR)(B−ΔC)(−dCdt)=−ϕdUdt.\boxed{ P_{\text{effective}} = \phi \left(\frac{C}{R}\right) (B-\Delta C) \left(-\frac{dC}{dt}\right) = -\phi\frac{dU}{dt}. }

This says:

The stored potential UU is being depleted at rate −dU/dt-dU/dt, and ϕ\phi determines what fraction of that depletion appears as useful output.
